## Decision
- `scripts/build-app.sh` resolves `~/Applications` and exits with an error if the build directory is the same. Otherwise `install` would delete the build it is about to copy. If the directory was created by this run, it is removed first.
- `scripts/test-install.sh` runs with a fake `HOME`. It now exports the real Go module cache, build cache and GOPATH, so Go does not download modules into the temp directory and build cold there.
- The cleanup trap runs `chmod -R u+w` before `rm -rf`, because module-cache files are read-only.
- A new test case checks that `install.sh` with the build directory set to the fake `~/Applications` fails, and that the installed app's marker file is untouched.

